To decompose the mission into a goal model for a multi-robot system, we need to identify the high-level goals and break them down into sub-goals and tasks. Here's a structured breakdown:

### Goal Model

#### Goals

| Goal ID | Goal Title                  | Text                                                                 | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
| ------- | --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | --------- | -------- |
| G1      | Complete Resource Delivery  | Ensure all required resources are collected and delivered.           | -                  | Achieve   | -        |
| G2      | Collect Resources           | Gather all specified resources from storage locations.               | #                  | Perform   | G1       |
| G3      | Deliver Resources           | Deliver collected resources to the specified location.               | #                  | Perform   | G1       |
| G4      | Manage Battery Levels       | Ensure robots manage battery levels during missions.                 | -                  | Achieve   | G1       |
| G5      | Handle Collection Battery   | Manage battery during resource collection phase.                    | -                  | Achieve   | G4       |
| G6      | Handle Delivery Battery     | Manage battery during resource delivery phase.                      | -                  | Achieve   | G4       |
| G7      | Assign Missions on Low Battery | Reassign missions if battery is low during collection or delivery. | -                  | Perform   | G5, G6   |
| G8      | Trigger Alert on Failure    | Trigger alert if resource return to checkpoint fails.                | -                  | Perform   | G6       |

#### Tasks

| Task ID | Task Title                    | Text                                                                 | Relation | Location          | Number of Robots |
| ------- | ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ----------------- | ---------------- |
| AT1     | Navigate to Storage           | Move to the storage location for resource collection.                | AND      | Storage Locations | [1, n]           |
| AT2     | Request Resource              | Send message to storage for resource retrieval.                      | AND      | Storage Locations | 1                |
| AT3     | Retrieve Resource             | Wait for and retrieve the specified resources.                       | AND      | Storage Locations | 1                |
| AT4     | Navigate to Delivery Location | Move to the specified delivery location with collected resources.    | AND      | Delivery Location | [1, n]           |
| AT5     | Deliver Resource              | Deliver resources to the specified location.                         | AND      | Delivery Location | 1                |
| AT6     | Return to Recharge            | Navigate to recharging station if battery is low during collection.  | AND      | Recharge Station  | 1                |
| AT7     | Reassign Mission              | Reassign task to another robot if battery is low.                    | AND      | N/A               | 1                |
| AT8     | Return to Checkpoint          | Return resource to checkpoint if battery is low during delivery.     | AND      | Checkpoint        | 1                |
| AT9     | Trigger Alert                 | Send alert to sector manager if resource return fails.               | AND      | N/A               | 1                |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**: Both collection and delivery must be completed.
- **G2 -> AT1, AT2, AT3 [AND]**: Each step in resource collection is necessary.
- **G3 -> AT4, AT5 [AND]**: Each step in resource delivery is necessary.
- **G4 -> G5, G6 [AND]**: Both battery management phases must be addressed.
- **G5 -> AT6, AT7 [AND]**: Manage battery during collection.
- **G6 -> AT8, AT9 [AND]**: Manage battery during delivery.
- **G7 -> AT6, AT7 [AND]**: Reassign mission if battery is low.
- **G8 -> AT9 [AND]**: Trigger alert if resource return fails.

This model ensures that all aspects of the mission are covered, with clear roles and responsibilities for each robot involved.
